The midterm was worth 30 points.  Each of the 6 questions was worth 5 points.  The solutions have already been provided since these questions were all provided earlier in the course.\
\
The grading scheme is below\
\
1.  2.5 points for each direction of the proof. Otherwise graded with respect to the grading rubric proof (see file in this same folder) with respect to correctness and clearness of communication.\
\
2. 1 point for listing out the possible combinations of truth values for the two propositions.   2 points for having the correct columns in the truth table corresponding to each side of the equation.  1 point for showing your work on how you obtained those columns.  1 point for conclusion.\
\
3. 2.5 points for each subpart.  3/5 points were awarded if you switched the solutions.  4/5 points were awarded if you divided the correct answers by 3!.   2.5/5 points were awarded if you mixed up the notation for the falling factorial with the notation for the binomial coefficient, or if you added instead of multiplied.\
\
4. 1 point for breaking down A=B into \'93A is a subset of B\'94 and \'93B is a subset of A\'94.   2 points for correctly justifying each subset inclusion.\
\
5. 3 points for stating that the relation is not an equivalence relation due to the failure of symmetry.  2 points for justifying why.\
\
6. 2.5 points for each subpart.    Half credit was awarded if you forgot to divide by 10 to account for the equivalence class induced by the circles. \
